The base is zune-jpeg 0.5.15 as crates.io publishes it: the crate's `.cargo_vcs_info.json` names
that commit, its `src/` is byte for byte the published one, and upstream tags no 0.5.15. The paths
below are the crate's own, so the patch applies in the repository with
`git apply --directory=crates/zune-jpeg`. Carried by the owner's fork `close2/zune-image`, branch
`pdf-viewer/0.5.15-with-fixes`, at `1c7d01b8`, which the root Cargo.toml pins: doc/questions/Q227,
answered (ADRs 1589, 1730). The upstream report is the `.md` beside this file.
Found by the `jpeg_bands` fuzz target (ADR 1495). `decode_dc` already updates the DC prediction
with `wrapping_add`; the dequantising multiply beside it does not, so a frame whose accumulated DC
prediction leaves i32 range once multiplied by the quantiser's DC entry panics wherever overflow
checks are on (the dev, test and fuzz profiles) and wraps in release. This makes the multiply wrap
as the addition does, which is release's behaviour in every profile. The reproduction is the
846-byte codestream below (hexadecimal), a 2122 x 509 one-component frame decoded whole to RGBA;
`crates/pdf-model/tests/banded_decodes.rs`'s
`a_dc_prediction_past_i32_is_decoded_rather_than_aborting` holds it as a regression test:
